# AWS-0039 — EKS Kubernetes 1.36
# AWS enables envelope encryption by default for EKS 1.28+.
# Uses an AWS-owned KMS key; no custom encryption_config required.
# Reference: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/envelope-encryption.html
AVD-AWS-0039

# AWS-0040 / AWS-0041 — EKS public API access
# Accepted for this development sandbox only.
# Public API access is intentional for kubectl from a trusted /32 IP.
# Private API access remains enabled.
# Review before production deployment.

AVD-AWS-0040
AVD-AWS-0041

# AWS-0104 — EKS node outbound HTTPS
# OPEN RISK: Nodes permit HTTPS egress to 0.0.0.0/0 via NAT.
# Required for current NAT-based AWS service connectivity.
# Review destination restrictions before deployment.
# Do not suppress this finding until the risk is explicitly accepted.